# Audio Extractor

Download audio at the highest quality from YouTube, SoundCloud, Bandcamp, and 1000+ other sites.

## Install

```bash
# Clone / cd into the project folder, then:
pip install -e .

# ffmpeg is also required:
sudo pacman -S ffmpeg        # Manjaro / Arch
# or: brew install ffmpeg    # macOS
# or: sudo apt install ffmpeg
```

## Usage

```bash
# Open the GUI (default when no URL given)
audio-extractor
audio-extractor --ui

# Headless / CLI
audio-extractor "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=..."
audio-extractor "https://soundcloud.com/artist/track" --format mp3
audio-extractor "https://..." --output ~/Music --format flac
```

## Update

Since it's installed in editable mode (`-e`), any edits to `audio_extractor.py`
take effect immediately — no reinstall needed.

To bump the version and do a clean reinstall:

```bash
# edit version in pyproject.toml, then:
pip install -e . --force-reinstall
```

## Config

Settings (colours, font size, output dir) are saved to:
```
~/.config/audio_extractor/settings.json
```

## Options

| Flag | Default | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `--format`, `-f` | `best` | Output format: best, flac, wav, mp3, aac, opus, m4a, vorbis |
| `--quality`, `-q` | `0` | Quality for lossy formats (mp3: 0=best…9, aac/opus: kbps) |
| `--output`, `-o` | `./downloads` | Output directory |
| `--no-playlist` | on | Download single track, not whole playlist |
| `--ui` | — | Force open the GUI |

## Environment variables (.env)

```env
FORMAT=mp3
OUTPUT_FOLDER=~/Music
```